ble Update Policies**: Allows users to customize their update schedules and thresholds. - **Performance Tuning**: - **Advanced CPU Profiling**: Performance profiling tools enhance system performance tuning. - **Virtualization Support**: Enhanced virtualization capabilities to optimize resource utilization. - **Disk Management**: - **Partitioning**: Advanced partitioning options improve disk space efficiency. - **File System Optimizations**: File system optimizations reduce disk usage and improve performance. - **Security Features**: - **Kernel Security Modules**: Kernel-level security mechanisms enhance system security. - **Anti-Virus Software**: Advanced antivirus solutions ensure safe browsing environments. - **Operating System**: - **Enhanced Security**: Increased security features include enhanced security patches and updated firmware. - **Security Audits**: Regular security audits help identify and mitigate vulnerabilities. - **Software Distribution**: - **Distribute RPMs**: Red Hat Enterprise Linux 9 supports RPM-based distribution formats. - **Binary Packages**: Improved binary package development tools support modern programming languages. #### 2. **User Interface and Tools** - **Web Console**: - **Admin Console**: Offers a user-friendly interface for managing system configurations and operations. - **Interactive Dashboards**: Interactive dashboards allow administrators to monitor system health and performance in real-time.
